Subject: [URGENT] Helm Chart 1.18.3 Memory Regression — Hotfix 1.18.4 Available
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 04:15:00 +0000
Message-ID: <vendor-hotfix-001@k8s-vendor.example.com>

Team,

We have identified a critical memory regression introduced in chart version
1.18.3 released on 2026-05-13. The default memory limit in values.yaml was
inadvertently reduced from 2048Mi to 512Mi during an automated template
refactor. This change was not caught by our CI suite because the integration
test cluster has more permissive resource quotas.

The affected chart version is 1.18.3. If you are running this version,
your payment-svc pods will be subject to OOM kills under normal production
load.

We have published emergency hotfix 1.18.4 to our chart repository with the
following change:

  resources:
    limits:
      memory: 2048Mi    # restored from incorrectly reduced 512Mi

Please upgrade immediately using:
  helm upgrade payment-svc vendor-charts/payment-svc --version 1.18.4 -n payments

The full release notes are attached in your workspace.

Sincerely,
Vendor Release Engineering
releases@k8s-vendor.example.com
